        "explanation": "Detection-as-code with Sigma gives portability (one rule converts to KQL, SPL, Elastic), a version-controlled and reviewable history, testing before deployment, and community sharing — turning detections into durable, reproducible engineering artifacts rather than fragile console clicks that vanish when their author leaves. Option a dismisses those concrete benefits. Option c invents a runtime-performance claim; Sigma is authoring-time, then converted to native queries. Option d is false — no format proves a detection correct or free of false positives."
